---

# Requirements

Each article idea MUST include:

## 1. Title
A compelling, professional, non-clickbait title.

## 2. Core Problem
Explain the real engineering problem or challenge the article addresses.

## 3. Fundamental Concept
Explain which engineering fundamental(s) the article strengthens, such as:
- Separation of concerns
- Coupling vs cohesion
- Scalability
- State management
- Reliability
- Concurrency
- System boundaries
- Domain modeling
- Maintainability
- Performance
- Observability
- Communication patterns
- API design
- Fault tolerance

## 4. Technology Focus
Mention the relevant stack or technologies involved:
- React
- TypeScript
- Node.js
- NestJS
- PostgreSQL
- Redis
- Kafka
- React Native
- Docker
- Monorepo tooling
- etc.

## 5. Architecture Perspective
Explain the architectural angle or trade-off discussion:
Examples:
- Monolith vs microservice
- EDA vs request-response
- Microfrontend trade-offs
- Modular monolith advantages
- When abstraction becomes harmful
- Scaling organizational complexity

## 6. Skill Level
Label:
- Intermediate
- Advanced
- Senior-level

## 7. Why This Topic Matters
Explain why this topic is important in modern engineering environments.

## 8. Suggested Article Structure
Provide a concise outline with sections/subsections.

